WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.512 --> 00:00:03.072
This is the northern bald eagle.

00:00:04.608 --> 00:00:06.144
An iconic bird

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.728
that we almost lost for good only a few decades ago,

00:00:09.984 --> 00:00:14.080
northern bald eagles are the larger of the two subspecies of the bald eagle.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.920
Their wingspan can reach over seven feet.

00:00:18.944 --> 00:00:26.000
They are powerful flyers that soar through the air, reaching over 40 miles per hour when gliding.

00:00:26.368 --> 00:00:31.000
They’re excellent predators, attacking from above with their long and sharp talons.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.072
By the 1960s, their population was decimated

00:00:35.584 --> 00:00:38.400
with less than 1000 left in the wild.

00:00:39.168 --> 00:00:44.544
Chemicals from pesticides traveled up the food chain rendering these top predators sterile

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.592
or unable to lay healthy eggs.

00:00:47.104 --> 00:00:52.224
Thankfully, after massive regulations were put in place they have made a near full recovery.

00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:56.064
Today, loss of suitable habitat is still a threat

00:00:56.576 --> 00:01:00.672
as they are very sensitive to human activity.

00:01:00.928 --> 00:01:03.744
This is the northern bald eagle.

